id: pm-rust-cqk7
title: Persist native close resolution and completion metadata with oracle parity
description: "Match all published close metadata flags, validation, canonical history and JSON/TOON envelopes using real disposable tracker differentials."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: conformance,mutation,rust
created_at: "2026-10-14T20:34:22.844Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-15T01:50:26.156Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Every close help field and alias has real oracle differential coverage; regression tests fail on behavioral reversion; unchanged complete Rust gates pass.
parent: pm-rust-u4al
comments[10]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-14T20:34:38.624Z",codex-agent,"Implementing the native parity batch against the locked 2026.10.14 oracle. Evidence will compare real disposable trackers, complete output envelopes and durable artifacts, with a behavioral revert proof and unchanged release gates."
  "2026-10-14T20:55:48.342Z",codex-agent,"Real tracker differentials now prove successful close fields and aliases in JSON and TOON, timestamp overrides and preservation, duplicate fallbacks, explicit forced repeat closure and assignment release. Refusal comparisons include exact recovery command quoting, canonical alias arguments and explicit completion flag/value diagnostics. Additional governance and child validation scenarios and complete coverage gates are in progress."
  "2026-10-14T21:33:38.626Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: cargo test --locked --test close_differential close_fields_aliases_and_formats_match_oracle -- --exact --nocapture compiled and failed at runtime with exit 101. Restoring only close_item loses inline closure metadata; exact item/history artifact comparison fails. The regression test stayed in place, and all source bytes were restored after the check."
  "2026-10-14T22:40:01.966Z",codex-agent,"The item-linked pinned-oracle command passed through pm test --run --only-last --progress --fail-on-skipped --fail-on-empty-test-run --json: 5 tests passed, zero failures or skips. Test-result tracking is disabled by project policy, so this append-only comment records the observed receipt. The behavioral revert failure is recorded separately. Assignment-release coverage also compares exact combined field counts, null omission in TOON, retained completion time, repeated aliases and durable closure when a subsequent stale session lock refuses release."
  "2026-10-14T23:04:19.910Z",codex-agent,"Both full runs passed 314 tests with zero failures or ignored tests. The unchanged coverage floor then identified untested title clipping, a post-item history-publication failure and a non-relative malformed date. Added real filesystem recovery verification and oracle comparisons for long duplicate diagnostics and malformed dates; narrowed the private refusal constructor to its actual String input. A fresh final aggregate is still required before delivery."
  "2026-10-14T23:22:32.085Z",codex-agent,"The expanded five-group close differential suite passes after matching the oracle unknown_error JSON and exit 1 for relative-date overflow. Compact calendars, malformed date components, long refusal titles and recoverable history-publication failure are now covered. Follow-up pm-rust-9bci records the upstream diagnostic for reassessment after a future oracle pin update; no pin or threshold changed."
  "2026-10-14T23:57:23.246Z",codex-agent,"Foreign-owner differentials exposed preset validation precedence: minimal resolves to off, default to warn, strict to strict, and custom uses its explicit close-validation override or warn. Native now matches that effective settings behavior. Verification also covers two-child ordering, preserved predecessor edges, nominal SDK hours/days/weeks and TOON null omission. The close suite is organized into six groups to retain deny-warnings Clippy without relaxing any gate."
  "2026-10-15T00:18:36.991Z",codex-agent,"All remaining SDK boundary checks pass: duplicate target refusal, invalid validation and completion propagation leave item/history bytes unchanged; duplicate fallback preserves supplied resolution; an owner closes their own claim without force. Supplementing the same production source profile now measures 100 percent lines, regions, functions and branches. A fresh aggregate is running next so the final acceptance receipt does not rely on accumulated profiles."
  "2026-10-15T00:40:00.752Z",codex-agent,"Final Linux acceptance: just release-check passed at unchanged pins and thresholds in an isolated Git identity environment. Both the ordinary and fresh branch-instrumented suites passed 317 tests across 17 targets, with zero failures or ignored tests. Coverage: 5646/5646 lines, 8630/8630 regions, 522/522 functions and 1194/1194 branches, all 100 percent. Formatting, deny-warnings Clippy, private-item rustdoc, identity audit, locked-oracle differential suites, cargo audit and changelog check passed. Cargo audit retains the inherited allowed RUSTSEC-2024-0449 unmaintained advisory. Per-item behavioral revert proof and linked-test receipts remain recorded separately. Releasing ownership for orchestrator verification; this item remains in progress and is not closed. The final item-linked command passed all six close groups, including preset validation defaults, duplicate evidence preservation, predecessor cleanup, assignment release and overflow diagnostics."
  "2026-10-15T01:50:26.156Z",claude-hub,"Windows CI fix by the orchestrator (2026-10-15). On windows-latest three close differential tests failed. The suggested_retry in close_validation_missing_fields spelled the tracker as the canonical verbatim path (the \\\\?\\ prefix plus the long user directory name), while the Node oracle prints the path as the process sees it (path.resolve, keeping the 8.3 short name). close_item now takes the workspace's query_pm_root (the Node-style lexical path on Windows; identical to the canonical root on Linux) and uses it only for the recovery hint; all filesystem work still uses the canonical root. Unit test close_recovery_spells_the_display_root_not_the_canonical_root fails when the hint uses the canonical root (revert proof). The same commit restores the platform-independent assert_cmd import that the earlier reordering had gated to Linux. just release-check passes locally: tests, 100 percent lines, regions, functions and branches, clippy with deny warnings (also for the x86_64-pc-windows-gnu target), audit, identity and changelog."
